; The fake root. Signed; its KSK is the only trust anchor the validating
; resolver holds.
;
; A real signed root is used rather than an explicit trust-anchor for a fake TLD
; because the interaction between Unbound's `trust-anchor:` and `domain-insecure:`
; is version-dependent, and because only a genuinely signed parent makes
; DNSSEC_INSECURE_ISLAND ("signed parent, delegation carries no DS") reproducible.
;
; ns0.test. is glue for a name inside the delegated test. zone, which is exactly
; how the real root works — root servers live under the delegated root-servers.net.
$ORIGIN .
$TTL 3600

@       IN SOA  ns0.test. hostmaster.propgate.invalid. (
                1          ; serial
                7200       ; refresh
                3600       ; retry
                1209600    ; expire
                3600 )     ; minimum
@       IN NS   ns0.test.

; test. is delegated to dns-root itself (127.0.0.2), which serves both zones.
test.           IN NS   ns0.test.
ns0.test.       IN A    127.0.0.2

; DS records below are injected by scripts/sign.sh. Do not edit by hand.
; BEGIN GENERATED DS
test.			IN DS 53725 8 2 E747D2F402F8522E011A38E1522E313BEAF7F3040AE318B326B7A795 365F18C2
; END GENERATED DS
